{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00507",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.76,
      "end_seconds": 13.73,
      "duration_seconds": 12.97,
      "text": "Come in, take a seat. The nurse has had a quick word and says you're here about your hair, but I'd rather hear it in your own words."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.99,
      "end_seconds": 17.79,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "Yeah. It's thinning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.23,
      "end_seconds": 25.3,
      "duration_seconds": 6.07,
      "text": "Thinning where, would you say? All over, or in one patch?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 27.05,
      "end_seconds": 32.45,
      "duration_seconds": 5.4,
      "text": "The top, mostly. The crown, where my parting is."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 34.64,
      "end_seconds": 38.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.14,
      "text": "And how long have you noticed it for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 41.4,
      "end_seconds": 43.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Six months. About that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.55,
      "end_seconds": 56.06,
      "duration_seconds": 9.51,
      "text": "Was there something that made you spot it, or did it just creep up on you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.98,
      "end_seconds": 66.77,
      "duration_seconds": 8.79,
      "text": "My wife pointed it out. Then I saw the photos from my sister's wedding and, well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.95,
      "end_seconds": 79.69,
      "duration_seconds": 10.74,
      "text": "Right. Is it more that hairs are falling out, or that they're getting finer so you can see more scalp through them?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.33,
      "end_seconds": 89.63,
      "duration_seconds": 7.3,
      "text": "Both, a bit. It's coming out in handfuls when I wash it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.62,
      "end_seconds": 97.55,
      "duration_seconds": 6.93,
      "text": "Handfuls in the shower. Is that every wash, or just now and then?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.41,
      "end_seconds": 100.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "Every wash."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 101.81,
      "end_seconds": 128.59,
      "duration_seconds": 26.78,
      "text": "Okay. Think of your scalp like a lawn. Each hair grows for years, rests, drops out, and a new one starts from the same spot. Something can nudge a lot of them into the resting phase together, and then you lose a clump at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.53,
      "end_seconds": 131.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.11,
      "text": "Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.62,
      "end_seconds": 148.34,
      "duration_seconds": 13.72,
      "text": "The other pattern is more like a lawn slowly going thin because every blade comes back a little finer each season. That one is down to the follicle itself."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.07,
      "end_seconds": 154.19,
      "duration_seconds": 4.12,
      "text": "Is that the one I've got?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.14,
      "end_seconds": 175.14,
      "duration_seconds": 20.0,
      "text": "I'd be guessing if I said, and I'd rather not guess at you. What I can tell you is that there are sensible things we can do whichever it turns out to be."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.12,
      "end_seconds": 179.64,
      "duration_seconds": 1.52,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.49,
      "end_seconds": 198.11,
      "duration_seconds": 16.62,
      "text": "Before anything else, a blood test makes sense. I'd like to check your iron stores and your thyroid, because both can quietly affect hair and both are easy to put right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.25,
      "end_seconds": 203.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Fine. When would that be?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.45,
      "end_seconds": 218.51,
      "duration_seconds": 12.06,
      "text": "The nurse can take it on your way out today. It's about two minutes with a needle, no fasting needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 219.54,
      "end_seconds": 220.63,
      "duration_seconds": 1.09,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 222.31,
      "end_seconds": 237.07,
      "duration_seconds": 14.76,
      "text": "Meanwhile I'm going to start you on minoxidil foam. Carrying on with the lawn idea, it's a bit like fertiliser: it wakes the follicles up and lengthens their growing phase."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 238.48,
      "end_seconds": 242.72,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "Do I put it on wet hair?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.71,
      "end_seconds": 255.4,
      "duration_seconds": 11.69,
      "text": "Dry scalp is best. Once a day, half a capful, rubbed in wherever it's thin, then wash your hands thoroughly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 256.38,
      "end_seconds": 258.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Once a day. Right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.13,
      "end_seconds": 277.82,
      "duration_seconds": 17.69,
      "text": "Be warned, it can make you shed a bit more for the first month or so. That's the old resting hairs making way, and it's a good sign rather than a bad one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 280.1,
      "end_seconds": 282.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Hm. So worse first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.6,
      "end_seconds": 296.13,
      "duration_seconds": 11.53,
      "text": "A little worse first, yes. Most people need around four months before they see any difference, so please don't judge it too early."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 298.03,
      "end_seconds": 299.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Four months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.89,
      "end_seconds": 318.06,
      "duration_seconds": 17.17,
      "text": "Take a photo of your crown in the same light today, and then again every month. It's far more reliable than trusting your memory in the bathroom mirror."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 319.44,
      "end_seconds": 322.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "I can do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 324.58,
      "end_seconds": 336.94,
      "duration_seconds": 12.36,
      "text": "And be kind to what you've got: no harsh brushing or tight hats. Ordinary shampoo is fine, you don't need anything fancy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 338.26,
      "end_seconds": 340.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "Not a problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 342.15,
      "end_seconds": 348.07,
      "duration_seconds": 5.92,
      "text": "Good. Did you want to ask me anything before you go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 349.88,
      "end_seconds": 353.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Will the bloods take long to come back?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 356.69,
      "end_seconds": 363.76,
      "duration_seconds": 7.07,
      "text": "Usually a few days. The results will be on your record by then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 365.56,
      "end_seconds": 367.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Right. Thanks, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 370.39,
      "end_seconds": 376.13,
      "duration_seconds": 5.74,
      "text": "You're welcome. Mind the step on your way out."
    }
  ]
}
